2024-46859}\n   * CVE-2025-38198\n     - fbcon: Introduce wrapper for console->fb_info lookup\n       {CVE-2025-38198}\n     - fbcon: Use fbcon_info_from_console() in\n       fbcon_modechange_possible() {CVE-2025-38198}\n     - fbcon: Make sure modelist not set on unregistered console\n       {CVE-2025-38198}\n   * CVE-2025-38702\n     - fbdev: fix potential buffer overflow in do_register_framebuffer()\n       {CVE-2025-38702}\n   * CVE-2025-40135\n     - ipv6: use RCU in ip6_xmit() {CVE-2025-40135}\n   * CVE-2025-40158\n     - ipv6: use RCU in ip6_output() {CVE-2025-40158}\n   * CVE-2025-71082\n     - Bluetooth: btusb: revert use of devm_kzalloc in btusb\n       {CVE-2025-71082}\n   * CVE-2026-43250\n     - usb: chipidea: udc: fix DMA and SG cleanup in _ep_nuke()\n       {CVE-2026-43250}\n   * CVE-2026-45893\n     - apparmor: Fix & Optimize table creation from possibly unaligned\n       memory {CVE-2026-45893}\n   * CVE-2026-46254\n     - AppArmor: Allow apparmor to handle unaligned dfa tables\n       {CVE-2026-46254}\n   * CVE-2026-53224\n     - sctp: validate embedded INIT chunk and address list lengths in\n       cookie {CVE-2026-53224}\n   * CVE-2026-53246\n     - sctp: validate cached peer INIT chunk length in COOKIE_ECHO\n       processing {CVE-2026-53246}\n   * CVE-2026-63983\n     - net: Introduce skb tc depth field to track packet loops\n       {CVE-2026-63983}\n     - net/sched: fix packet loop on netem when duplicate is on\n       {CVE-2026-63983}\n   * CVE-2026-68108\n     - drm/amdgpu/vce: fix integer overflow in image size\n       {CVE-2026-68108}\n   * CVE-2026-68329\n     - iommu/amd: Wait for completion instead of returning early in\n       iommu_completion_wait() {CVE-2026-68329}\n   * CVE-2026-74310\n     - vhost/net: complete zerocopy ubufs only once {CVE-2026-74310}\n   * CVE-2026-74454\n     - drm/vc4: Supply the overflow slot size in BPOS, not the whole bin\n       BO size {CVE-2026-74454}\n   * CVE-2026-74689\n     - net: Make copy_safe_from_sockptr() match documentation\n       {CVE-2026-74689}\n     - net/atm: fix slab-out-of-bounds read in vcc_setsockopt()\n       {CVE-2026-74689}\n   * CVE-2026-74752\n     - sctp: validate cookie AUTH state before use {CVE-2026-74752}\n   * CVE-2026-80576\n     - drm/amdgpu: reject oversized IBs with per-ring packet limits\n       {CVE-2026-80576}\n   * CVE-2026-90116\n     - ALSA: mtpav: shut down output timer before card teardown\n       {CVE-2026-90116}\n   * CVE-2026-92508\n     - RDMA/core: Fix potential use after free in ib_free_cq()\n       {CVE-2026-92508}\n   * CVE-2026-92509\n     - RDMA/core: Fix potential use after free in counter_release()\n       {CVE-2026-92509}\n   * CVE-2026-93104\n     - RDMA/rvt: Return NULL after port allocation failure\n       {CVE-2026-93104}\n   * CVE-2026-93117\n     - usb: fix UAF when probe runs concurrent to dyn ID removal\n       {CVE-2026-93117}\n   * CVE-2026-97493\n     - drm/amdgpu: Bound GPIO I2C table entry count from VBIOS\n       {CVE-2026-97493}\n   * CVE-2026-97541\n     - wifi: ath9k_htc: don't store usb_device_id {CVE-2026-97541}\n   * CVE-2026-98176\n     - drm/amdkfd: Avoid integer underflow with ffs in EOP ring size calc\n       {CVE-2026-98176}\n   * CVE-2026-98213\n     - mmc: core: Cancel SDIO IRQ work before freeing host\n       {CVE-2026-98213}\n   * CVE-2026-98428\n     - ALSA: usb: 6fire: Avoid embedded URBs {CVE-2026-98428}\n   * Miscellaneous upstream changes\n     - xen-netback: Fix UAF when reading statistics data\n     - xen-netback: defer xenvif_mcast_addr_list_free()\n     - xen-blkback: Avoid UAF when reading I/O statistics\n     - Linux 5.10.274","affected":[{"package":{"name":"bpftool","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Debian:11","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/bpftool?distro=debian-11"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"5.10.274-1+tuxcare.els1"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/debian11els/CLSA-2026-1794339348.